    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Conclusion'>
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='46954' id='3' type-v2='text' w='54355' x='22473' y='29123'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#e15759' fontsize='24'>Conclusion</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The analysis reveals several notable trends in the Airbnb landscape of New York City. Manhattan and Brooklyn emerge as the most active areas for Airbnb listings, both in terms of volume and pricing. The data shows that a significant portion of high-priced listings are managed by professional or corporate hosts, with some listings reaching price levels as high as $80,000. Entire home or apartment listings are the most common room type and are usually priced higher than private or shared rooms. Furthermore, there is evidence suggesting that higher review frequency and greater availability are associated with better listing performance. These factors appear to contribute to increased visibility and possibly higher revenue for hosts. Overall, this analysis highlights how location, listing attributes, and host behavior collectively influence the Airbnb market in NYC.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
